As I understand it, you can calculate EVC and PUC after you fit the bifactor model (as the difference between the factor loadings between the unidimensional model and the bifactor model is what is used by the computation).

Use BifactorIndicesCalculator package in R.

Also see: The Bifactor Indices Calculator by Michael Toland is available from https://uknowledge.uky.edu/edp_tools/1/ <https://www.youtube.com/redirect?q=https%3A%2F%2Fuknowledge.uky.edu%2Fedp_tools%2F1%2F&redir_token=HEZaikiV3AD66hocirte1ca3KZJ8MTU5NDMzNjQ2MEAxNTk0MjUwMDYw&event=video_description&v=8E3S_rVofV0> (Citation: https://doi.org/10.13023/edp.tool.01 <https://www.youtube.com/redirect?q=https%3A%2F%2Fdoi.org%2F10.13023%2Fedp.tool.01&redir_token=HEZaikiV3AD66hocirte1ca3KZJ8MTU5NDMzNjQ2MEAxNTk0MjUwMDYw&event=video_description&v=8E3S_rVofV0>)

